    "notes": "The west-facing Arminius and his raised sword stand over the ten-pier sandstone arcade. Two curved eastern flights climb to a shared landing and a short upper stair. The new foundation follows the sampled slopes below the pedestal. The statue retains its published height and uses polygonal approximations of the face and clothing folds. The capital heads, waterspouts and stair profiles follow photographs and the mapped approach. Precise masonry, carving and riser dimensions are approximate."
